WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:09.250
According to a recent study, a small but growing proportion of the workforce is affected to some degree by a sense of entitlement.
根据最近的一项研究，劳动者中有一小部分人在某种程度上受到特权心态的影响，而且这部分人所占的比例还在不断上升。

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:14.360
Work is less about what they can contribute and more about what they can take.
对他们而言，工作与其说关乎自己能贡献什么，不如说关乎自己能索取什么。

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.850
It can lead to workplace dysfunction and diminish their own job satisfaction.
这种心态可能导致职场运转失常，并降低他们自身的工作满意度。

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:30.450
I’m not referring to employees who are legitimately dissatisfied with their employment conditions due to, say, being denied fair pay or flexible work practices.
我指的不是那些有正当理由对雇佣条件感到不满的员工，比如说，因为得不到公平的薪酬或无法采用灵活的工作方式而不满的人。

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:36.920
I’m talking about those who consistently believe they deserve special treatment and generous rewards.
我说的是那些始终认为自己理应得到特殊待遇和丰厚回报的人。

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.940
It’s an expectation that exists irrespective of their abilities or levels of performance.
无论他们的能力或业绩水平如何，这种期望都存在。

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:54.530
As a result of that discrepancy between the privileges they feel they’re owed and their actual performance, and of their inflated sense of self-worth, they don’t work as hard for their employer.
由于自认为应得的特权与实际业绩之间存在这种落差，再加上自我价值感过高，他们为雇主工作就没那么卖力。

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:57.300
They prefer instead to slack off.
相反，他们宁愿偷懒懈怠。

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:04.210
It’s a tendency which many scholars believe begins in childhood due to parents who overindulge their kids.
许多学者认为，这种倾向始于童年，原因是父母过度溺爱孩子。

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:09.660
This leads them to expect the same kind of spoilt treatment throughout their adult lives.
这导致他们成年以后也一直期望得到同样的娇惯待遇。

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:18.160
And yet despite how these employees feel, it’s obviously important for their manager to nonetheless find out how to keep them motivated.
然而，尽管这些员工抱有这样的心态，对他们的经理来说，弄清楚如何让他们保持积极性显然仍然很重要。

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.570
And, by virtue of that heightened motivation, performing well.
并且让他们凭借由此提高的积极性，保持良好的表现。

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:29.500
The research team from several American universities surveyed more than 240 individuals.
来自美国几所大学的研究团队调查了240多人。

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.110
They sampled managers as well as team members.
他们抽样调查的对象既有经理，也有团队成员。

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:40.300
Employee entitlement was measured by statements such as “I honestly feel I’m just more deserving than others.”
员工特权心态用诸如“说实话，我觉得自己就是比别人更有资格”这样的陈述来衡量。

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.920
The respondents had to rate the extent of their agreement.
受访者需要评定自己在多大程度上同意这些说法。

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:50.850
Employee engagement, meanwhile, was assessed with statements like “I really throw myself into my work.”
而员工敬业度则用“我真的全身心投入工作”之类的陈述来评估。

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:58.540
The findings revealed ethical leadership is precisely what alleviates the negative effects of employee entitlement.
研究结果表明，缓解员工特权心态负面影响的，恰恰是道德型领导。

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:07.030
That’s because rather than indulging employees or neglecting them, ethical leaders communicate very direct and clear expectations.
这是因为道德型领导者既不纵容员工，也不忽视员工，而是传达非常直接、明确的期望。

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:13.840
They also hold employees accountable for their behaviors and are genuinely committed to doing the right thing.
他们还要求员工为自己的行为负责，并真心致力于做正确的事。

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.850
Additionally, these leaders are consistent in their standards.
此外，这些领导者的标准始终如一。

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:22.210
They’re also less likely to deviate in how they treat employees.
在对待员工的方式上，他们出现偏差的可能性也更小。

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:31.490
This means, when confronted by an entitled team member, an ethical leader is significantly disinclined to accommodate their demands.
这意味着，道德型领导者在面对有特权心态的团队成员时，会明显不愿迁就对方的要求。

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:40.710
He or she will instead point out, constructively and tactfully, exactly how their inflated sense of deservingness is somewhat distorted.
相反，领导者会以建设性而又得体的方式，确切地指出对方过高的应得感在哪些方面有些扭曲。

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:50.190
He or she will then go further to explain the specific, and objective, criteria the employee must meet to receive their desired rewards.
接着，领导者还会进一步说明，这名员工必须达到哪些具体而客观的标准，才能获得自己想要的回报。

00:02:50.990 --> 00:03:00.690
This shift away from unrealistic expectations is successful because entitled employees feel more confident that ethical leaders will deliver on their promises.
这种摆脱不切实际期望的转变之所以成功，是因为有特权心态的员工更加确信，道德型领导者会兑现承诺。

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:04.900
This occurs because they’re perceived to be fair and trustworthy.
之所以会这样，是因为这些领导者被视为公平、值得信赖的人。

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:12.660
The researchers, however, exercise caution by warning that no one single response is the perfect remedy.
然而，研究人员保持谨慎，提醒说没有哪一种单一的应对措施是完美的解决办法。

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:18.580
But there’s no denying ethical leadership is at least a critical step in the right direction.
但不可否认的是，道德型领导至少是朝正确方向迈出的关键一步。
